A practical repair
session was held when the NWEB provided lecturers,
instructors and the necessary equipment. Middleton held a Christmas cookery demonstration;
had a talk and demonstration by Mrs. Chadwick on
‘Tupperware’—American all polythene kitchen ware;
talks by a member Mrs.

Wyllie, Manager of the Irwell Valley Water Board. Visits were made to the Cheshire Sterilized Milk Co.;
and the Radcliffe Fire Station. Wilmslow visited the Wedgewood factory and saw
ceramic ware being made, fired, painted and glazed.

